A||||5||fierocd||2.8 backfires and puffs black smoke||||1||
Z||000000||fierocd||08-27-2001||11:12 PM||||OK, with some help from the Forum, I got my car running OK except for 2 things.  It seems to lack power and after about 10 minutes of driving, it backfires and puffs out a huge cloud of black smoke.  It will run fine for another mile or so and then do the same thing.  I came up with code 33, changed the MAP sensor, ignition module, along with all the basic tune-up parts.  Any ideas on what to check/replace???  Any help is appreciated as I am leaving for Texas in 2 weeks and need to have the car running to make it down there.||||reg||1
Z||000001||fierocd||08-28-2001||10:54 AM||||Could an ignition module be 1/2 bad.  The reason I ask is because I changed my with a spare(used) one I had laying around and the car stopped stalling and the backfires don't seem as severe.  It only does this when the car gets warmed up so I was thinking maybe when this module got heated up is just wasn't as shot as the other one.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Joe Torma||08-28-2001||11:10 AM||||Someone else is having a similar problem.  Ignition module could be your problem.  Won't hurt to replace it.<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/simplesig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Spektrum-87GT||08-28-2001||12:32 PM||||check what these guys said, but my cherokee had a similar problem and it turned out to be the distributor. If your rpms are bouncing all over the place also, then the distributor is probably the culprit.||||reg||1
Z||000004||fierocd||08-28-2001||01:23 PM||||OK, I changed the ignition module and the pick-up coil.  Now the car doesn't seem to backfire at all.  I just drove it around for about 20 minutes with no popping or smoke.  The only problem now is the car is stalling again anytime I push in the clutch or stop.  I cut the exhaust after the cat to check if that was clogged, looks like someone already cleared it out for me!||||reg||1
Z||000005||SteveJ||08-28-2001||01:45 PM||||Put a search on for backfire.<P>Yes, MAP can do that.<P>Seems to me the Ogre said that if the MAP sensor was messed due to backfire then the MAT would also be toast.||||reg||1
